{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nReconciler parity bugs (3f04, 4b59, 32cc class: inverted link directions, asymmetric field handling) escape because per-field asymmetry POLICY lives scattered in code with no single declarative source: the should_propagate_removal gate (rebar.reducer._managed_refs) is imported at four separate reconciler sites, add-wins tag merging is an inline dedup in apply_inbound_records.py, and inbound_differ carries only a 2-entry field-NAME canonicalization map (_OUTBOUND_TO_INBOUND_FIELD). No enumerable \"field contract\" exists yet — this ticket CREATES it. The typed-transport half of this hardening already landed as bug cc77 (closed; Gerrit 1222-1225 merged) — do not duplicate it. Pagination-iterator consolidation was split out of this ticket into its own child (see discovered_from link) after plan review flagged the bundle.\n\n## Approach\n(1) MATERIALIZE the contract: new module src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_field_contract.py — a declarative registry enumerating each reconciled field with its symmetry class (bidirectional-roundtrip / add-wins / one-way-with-propagation-gate) plus references to its codec/gate (e.g. should_propagate_removal for managed refs, the tag dedup for add-wins). The module docstring records this as the cross-cutting registration contract for future fields, and a one-paragraph pointer is added to the reconciler section of docs/architecture.md so new call sites know to register (captures the new convention durably).\n(2) Property tests parameterized OFF the registry: tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_field_contract_properties.py. Coverage guard: the test module enumerates the reconciled fields handled by inbound_differ/apply_inbound_records and fails collection if any handled field lacks a registry entry (adding a field without declaring its class breaks the build). Per-class properties: roundtrip identity asserted ONLY for declared-bidirectional value codecs (status mapping, link inward/outward direction); add-wins fields get a merge-idempotence + no-removal property; one-way-gated fields get a gate-consulted property (behavior asserted consistent with should_propagate_removal through the real call path).\n(3) NO behavior refactor: the registry declares, tests assert code behavior MATCHES declarations. Rewiring call sites to import the registry is explicitly out of scope (follow-up candidate if drift recurs); this keeps the change additive and low-risk.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_field_contract.py (new, declarative registry)\n- tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_field_contract_properties.py (new)\n- docs/architecture.md (one-paragraph registration-contract note in the reconciler section)\n- OUT of scope: pagination iterators (split to sibling ticket), call-site rewiring, any transport work (cc77 landed).\n\n## Testing\nThe property tests are the deliverable. Mutation check before push: flip one declared symmetry class in the registry — the named field's property test must fail; delete one registry entry — collection must fail via the coverage guard.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] _field_contract.py registry exists; every reconciled field handled by the differ/apply path has a declared symmetry class; docstring + docs/architecture.md note record the registration contract.\n- [ ] Coverage guard fails collection for a handled-but-undeclared field (proven by the deletion mutation).\n- [ ] Roundtrip identity asserted only for declared-bidirectional codecs; add-wins and gated classes have their class-specific properties asserted through real call paths.\n- [ ] relates_to link recorded to cc77 (typed transport, already landed/closed) and discovered_from link on the split-out pagination child."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785771909621428001,"uuid":"b3ec149a-51a2-4b88-8bd1-932c621e47cd"}